  "status": "formal",
  "supportedClaim": "For real or complex Banach-valued X in W^{2,1}, the squared derivative mass at all selected roots except the first is at most twice the integral of ||X'|| ||X''||. The factor two is sharp and the first-root payment is necessary. For the declared perturbative common-band triangular class, the complete complex-target root mass is comparable to a^2 N^2 and its physical critical-log normalization tends to zero."
